cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the associated article and this repository."
title: "DERS: Dual-Execution Robotics Simulation on MuJoCo/MJX"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gao
    given-names: Chenkai
  - family-names: Li
    given-names: Mingcan
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-27
license: Apache-2.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23643769
repository-code: "https://github.com/Echo-wxy/ders-mjx"
abstract: >
  Implementation of dual-execution simulation for contact-rich robot
  manipulation: the executed transition is always the hard MuJoCo/MJX step,
  the derivative comes from a separately relaxed backward model, and a
  straight-through coupling returns the hard state bit for bit while passing
  the relaxed derivative. Includes the mechanism-specific relaxations, the
  residual network, the gradient estimators used as baselines, the experiment
  scripts and the analysis code.
keywords:
  - differentiable simulation
  - robot manipulation
  - contact dynamics
  - straight-through estimator
  - MuJoCo
  - MJX
